            <ArticleTitle>An issue of sensitivity. Use of analgesic gel in catheterizing women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>738-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Catheterisation is an invasive, and often painful procedure for women, yet the use of analgesic gel does not appear to be the norm. It does, however, have a number of benefits for patient and nurse.</AbstractText>
